| `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` (lines 125, 594, 1315, 1434, 1577, 1631, 1635, 2047) | `plumbing.NewBranchReferenceName(paths.MetadataBranchName)` / `plumbing.NewRemoteReferenceName("origin", paths.MetadataBranchName)` | `checkpoint.MetadataRef(ctx)` / `checkpoint.MetadataTrackingRef(ctx)`. The 3 read entry points (`ReadCommitted`, `ListCommitted`, `WriteCommitted`'s read-modify-write start) also call `checkpoint.PreserveV1History(ctx, repo)` immediately after opening the repo, swallowing errors at WARN. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/parse_tree.go:447` | Branch ref | `checkpoint.MetadataRef(ctx)`. Entry point also calls `checkpoint.PreserveV1History`. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go:239` | Guard `if branchName == paths.MetadataBranchName` | Unchanged — still excludes the legacy branch from shadow-branch enumeration on legacy repos; harmless on 1.1 repos because the metadata ref isn't under `refs/heads/`. |
